Description: no <linux/input-event-codes.h> on Jam OS
 hello-wayland includes Linux's input header for one name, BTN_LEFT (the
 left button's code in wl_pointer.button, 0x110). Jam OS's sysroot has no
 Linux UAPI headers yet (the Chromium plan's toolchain adds them), so the
 name is defined here instead.
Forwarded: not-needed (Jam OS has no Linux UAPI headers yet; upstream builds on Linux)
---
--- a/main.c
+++ b/main.c
@@ -6,7 +6,7 @@
 #include <unistd.h>
 #include <wayland-client.h>
 #include <wayland-client-protocol.h>
-#include <linux/input-event-codes.h>
+#define BTN_LEFT 0x110   /* <linux/input-event-codes.h>'s */
 
 #include "cat.h"
 #include "shm.h"
